---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Before publication: confirm the released app matches the privacy audit,
// complete the visible confirmation fields, and remove the draft notice.
// Confirm the intended audience before adding any children-specific wording.
// Website visitor data is outside this app policy's scope and needs a separate review.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | Redo"
  description="How Redo handles your saved processes, photos, reminders, timers, shared files and support messages."
  current="privacy"
  pageClass="privacy-page"
>
  <main class="privacy-main">
    <article class="site-container prose">

      <div class="prose__intro">
        <div>
          <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose__intro-copy">
          <p class="prose-lead">Your saved processes and photos are stored locally in Redo on your device. Optional features let you use Apple Reminders and system timers, share processes and prepare support emails. Device backups and the services you choose may store additional copies.</p>
          <p class="policy-effective"><strong>Effective date:</strong> 23 November 2026</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <h2 id="about-title">About this policy</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Redo is developed and operated by <strong>James Azzopardi</strong>. This policy covers the Redo app for iPhone and iPad, its timer extension and associated support communications.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="information-title">
        <h2 id="information-title">Information saved on your device</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Redo stores the information needed to save and follow your processes, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>process titles, summaries and icons;</li>
            <li>step titles, instructions and photos;</li>
            <li>timer settings and active timer details;</li>
            <li>dates and identifiers linking processes to their reminders; and</li>
            <li>local record identifiers and process creation, update and last-used dates.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Redo does not require an account or provide its own cloud synchronisation. Saved process content is not automatically sent to the developer.</p>
          <p>Your device backup may include app data, depending on your settings and backup service. Apple Reminders may also synchronise through your configured accounts.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="photos-title">
        <h2 id="photos-title">Photos and camera</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>You can select images using Apple’s system photo picker or take a photo with your camera. The picker gives Redo access to the images you select, rather than your entire photo library. Taking a photo requires camera permission.</p>
          <p>Selected and captured photos are processed on your device before being saved. Images imported in a <code>.redo</code> file may be stored as received. Imported or shared photos may retain embedded metadata, including location information.</p>
          <p>Deleting a photo from a process does not delete the original image from your photo library.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="reminders-title">
        <h2 id="reminders-title">Reminders and timers</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>If you use reminders, Redo requests full read and write access to Apple Reminders. It uses this permission to create, check, update and remove reminders associated with your processes.</p>
          <p>The process title, reminder dates and a standard note are passed to Apple Reminders. These records may synchronise through the accounts you have configured for Reminders.</p>
          <p>Step timers use Apple’s system alarm services and require permission. Timer details include the step title and duration. The title and countdown may appear on your Lock Screen or Dynamic Island, depending on your device and settings.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
        <h2 id="sharing-title">Sharing and importing processes</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Sharing creates a readable <code>.redo</code> file containing the process title, icon, summary, step instructions, timer durations and any included photos. Local record identifiers, creation and usage dates, reminder details and active timer state are not included.</p>
          <p>Redo does not encrypt the export file itself. Anyone with access to it can read its contents. You choose the app, service or recipient through the system share sheet, and their handling of the file is outside Redo’s control.</p>
          <p>Importing a <code>.redo</code> file creates an independent process stored locally in Redo. It does not delete or remain linked to the original file. Redo cannot revoke shared files or remove copies held by recipients or other services.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="support-title">
        <h2 id="support-title">Support messages</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>When configured, Redo’s contact feature prepares an optional email with app, build and iOS version details. Sending requires your action. If you send a message, the recipient receives your email address and the content and attachments you choose to include.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="tracking-title">
        <h2 id="tracking-title">Advertising and analytics</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Redo contains no advertising, cross-app tracking or third-party analytics tools. Local dates used to organise your processes are not sent to the developer as usage reports.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention-title">
        <h2 id="retention-title">Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Your saved processes remain in Redo until you delete them. You can remove individual processes, steps or photos, or use <strong>Delete All Saved Data</strong>.</p>
          <p>When deleting a process, Redo also attempts to remove its associated Apple Reminder and cancel its timers. Permission or system errors can prevent deletion from completing. If an error occurs, some local content or system records may remain.</p>
          <p>Deleting content in Redo does not remove exported files, recipient copies, original imported files, sent emails or device backups. Removal of associated reminders from synced accounts depends on those services.</p>
          <p>Redo attempts to remove temporary export files when sharing finishes. An interruption can leave temporary files behind. Deletion does not guarantee immediate physical erasure of every stored copy.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="choices-title">
        <h2 id="choices-title">Your choices and security</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>Photos, camera access, reminders, timers and sharing are optional. You choose which images to provide through the photo picker and can manage camera, Reminders and alarm permissions in your device Settings. Withdrawing permission may prevent related features or cleanup from working.</p>
          <p>Redo uses your device’s app storage and operating-system access controls. Choose carefully what you include in shared files and emails, as their protection also depends on the services and recipients you select.</p>
          <p>James Azzopardi cannot remotely access or delete process content stored only on your device. You can manage that content directly in Redo.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes-title">
        <h2 id="changes-title">Contact and policy updates</h2>
        <div class="prose__body">
          <p>The proposed privacy and support address is <a href="mailto:info@redoapp.com.au" class="contact-address">info@redoapp.com.au</a>.</p>
          <p>Updates to this policy will appear on this page with a revised effective date.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
